    "created_at": "2023-03-13T03:24:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-03-13T03:24:03Z",
    "body": "I use lxd => containers to run many instances of servers. When you create an instance, two users are created: ubuntu and root. The ubuntu user has sudo privileges without needing a password. For example you can run \"sudo ls\" or  \"sudo apt udpate\" or \"sudo apt install ...\" without needing a password.  \r\n\r\nI performed a quick test by trying to install using the following => this worked:\r\ncurl -sS https://starship.rs/install.sh | **sudo** sh\r\n\r\nOne strange note: the prompt now reads:\r\n⬢ [Systemd] ❯\r\n\r\nI assume this prompt is different because I am running in lxd. The prompt looks normal in my host machine.\r\n\r\nI performed an installation in a separate container => this time installing as root (not ubuntu) using:\r\ncurl -sS https://starship.rs/install.sh |  sh\r\n\r\nThis worked as well. And, It produced the same result (prompt: ⬢ [Systemd] ❯) after updating the ubuntu .bashrc.\r\n\r\nUnless the Prompt of (⬢ [Systemd] ❯) is concerning to you, I believe you can close this ticket. Thank you for the quick response!!",
