    "body": "@davidkna, late to the party but I'm not sure this is fully resolved yet. There seems to be something fishy here. This:\r\n\r\n```\r\nper@some-host:~$ sudo whoami\r\nroot\r\n```\r\n\r\n...i.e. passwordless sudo is enabled. But when I run the Starship installer, I get some weird password prompt despite my account not even having a password. 🤔 \r\n\r\n```\r\nper@some-host:~$ curl -sS https://starship.rs/install.sh | sh\r\n\r\n  Configuration\r\n> Bin directory: /usr/local/bin\r\n> Platform:      unknown-linux-musl\r\n> Arch:          x86_64\r\n\r\n> Tarball URL: https://github.com/starship/starship/releases/latest/download/starship-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz\r\n? Install Starship latest to /usr/local/bin? [y/N] y\r\n! Escalated permissions are required to install to /usr/local/bin\r\n[sudo] password for per:\r\nSorry, try again.\r\n```",
